Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.21,0:00:06.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.38,0:00:09.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is Resembool?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.30,0:00:12.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's awfully...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.59,0:00:15.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry it's too rural for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.47,0:00:19.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's still looking.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.85,0:00:21.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.60,0:00:25.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's been looking at me \Never since we were on the train.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.81,0:00:26.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can understand why, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.23,0:00:30.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a crime to be so beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.57,0:00:33.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.99,0:00:36.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're Sara, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.62,0:00:37.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You sure have grown up.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.62,0:00:39.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,N-No, I'm not!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.54,0:00:51.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For crying out loud, pretending to be someone he knows! That's the oldest...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.68,0:00:55.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sara...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.72,0:00:58.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was my mom's name...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.23,0:01:07.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's this? You said you were going to study in Rush Valley,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.77,0:01:10.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but you've been in Central this whole time?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.27,0:01:11.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.57,0:01:14.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've been keeping an eye on Ed and Al.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.32,0:01:15.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't say.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.32,0:01:18.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, when are those two coming back?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.70,0:01:24.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah, Grandma, I met someone in Rush Valley who said they knew you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.29,0:01:30.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Grandma, no one's home!\NNo one, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.00,0:01:32.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good grief...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.09,0:01:35.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just a moment, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.02,0:01:44.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wow, the power of love!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.93,0:01:46.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've come back, have you?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.60,0:01:50.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Pinako-san, I can't seem to locate my house.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.86,0:01:54.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your house, as such, is no longer...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.11,0:01:56.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Grandma, you know this man?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.86,0:01:59.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, right. You were still\Nso little, and all.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.62,0:02:03.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This man is Ed and Al's father.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.66,0:02:11.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, and coming back \Nafter being away for so long,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.00,0:02:11.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't seem to find my house.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.50,0:02:15.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.59,0:02:20.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those who obtain it are set free from the Law of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.14,0:02:24.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is no need to pay a price\Nin order to obtain something, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.06,0:02:29.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We sought it and found it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.51,0:04:25.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How come you're so fast?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.39,0:04:27.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.43,0:04:29.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My body just seems\Nawfully light for some reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.97,0:04:32.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you're tired,\Nshould we take a break?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.90,0:04:37.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We can't.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.36,0:04:41.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What you said before\Nwas probably the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.65,0:04:44.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,About Führer Bradley?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.28,0:04:48.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That man... the Führer...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.95,0:04:50.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is a homunculus!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.75,0:04:55.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This time, the Führer was\Ncommanding the mission.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.21,0:04:57.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't think it was Envy\Ntaking his place.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.17,0:05:01.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Besides, the Führer's secretary was a homunculus.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.30,0:05:04.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we go back to the military, you and I both would be...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.76,0:05:06.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then, Brother, sure enough, that secretary lady is—
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.05,0:05:07.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't say it!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.30,0:05:12.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But Sensei said that homunculi are made when a human transmutation fails.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.18,0:05:14.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I told you not to say it!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.74,0:05:28.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.70,0:05:31.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What was that just now?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.62,0:05:32.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A huge gate...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.12,0:05:35.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've seen it before, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.17,0:05:38.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, was that truth?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.50,0:05:42.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sensei said it was\Nsomething else, but yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.88,0:05:45.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How did that happen,\Nwhen all we did is touch?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.88,0:05:51.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As an alchemist, I must have unknowingly made the Philosopher's Stone react.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.56,0:05:55.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, do you believe it, then?\NThat I've become\Na Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.27,0:06:02.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't feel like that's\Nwhat happened myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.69,0:06:05.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After all, the Philosopher's Stone\Nwouldn't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.32,0:06:06.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nobody has ever seen one.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.99,0:06:09.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whatever form it takes, it wouldn't surprise me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.49,0:06:11.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But never mind that.\NDon't get too close to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.79,0:06:13.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.16,0:06:17.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we inadvertently touch again, it will spark another reaction with the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.75,0:06:22.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no sense in having you disappear before we can take your body back.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.09,0:06:29.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, where are we going?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.72,0:06:29.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Resembool.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.47,0:06:31.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's where the military will look first.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.85,0:06:35.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those homunculi are\Nsure to come after you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.39,0:06:37.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we're going to beat them,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.56,0:06:39.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,there's something\Nthat we have to get.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.20,0:07:01.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Kimbly was apparently confirmed dead\Nin front of that red light.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.21,0:07:04.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, at that moment, Scar was still alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.46,0:07:10.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It appears that the townspeople fled outside the city before the military rushed in.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.68,0:07:14.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've discovered an underground passage, and we're tracing where it leads now.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.81,0:07:18.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Does this mean they \Nweren't trying to resist?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.60,0:07:20.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Was their objective
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.48,0:07:23.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,to use the military as ingredients,\Nmaking the whole city a transmutation circle?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.61,0:07:25.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed and Al appear to be safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.44,0:07:29.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Several soldiers witnessed Ed outside the city.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.03,0:07:34.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They said that about an hour ago, Ed and Al were leaving the area.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.58,0:07:36.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Could they be continuing\Non their journey?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.83,0:07:37.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even so...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.83,0:07:42.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I doubt that they were helping Scar to create a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.79,0:07:43.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.26,0:07:52.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,28 dead, 67 seriously injured, including five officers.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.84,0:07:55.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are still over 900 others missing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.72,0:07:58.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We will conduct a thorough\Ninvestigation as to what happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.43,0:08:02.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is one person who\Nknows exactly what happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.98,0:08:04.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Scar, you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.36,0:08:06.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Fullmetal...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.57,0:08:09.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Elric brothers.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.49,0:08:13.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For what reason\Ndid they show up in Liore?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.66,0:08:15.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We believe that\Nthey were pursuing Scar.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.07,0:08:19.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why? Did he have orders\Nto subdue Scar?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.95,0:08:24.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, they were engaged in various\Nfields of inquiry and alchemic research.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.46,0:08:28.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They appeared in Liore\Nand had dealings with Scar.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.59,0:08:33.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Have as many as a thousand officers\Nand men become casualties as a result?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.84,0:08:37.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not as though he has a rope\Naround the Elric brothers' necks.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.10,0:08:41.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I would like to give them\Na chance to explain themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.52,0:08:45.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you saying you will\Napprehend them yourself?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.31,0:08:46.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.65,0:08:51.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But if you fail to catch them, {\i1}you{\i0} will be the one who will have to explain himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.49,0:08:53.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.74,0:09:01.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,According to my intelligence,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.91,0:09:07.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the Elric brothers might be fighting alongside a seditious element that calls themselves homunculi.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.83,0:09:09.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Catch him and bring him back.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.67,0:09:13.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If it gets out of hand,\NI grant you permission to pass judgment on him on the spot.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.18,0:09:20.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.18,0:09:20.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You heard what he said.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.81,0:09:23.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sort through all the information we have\Non sightings of the Elric brothers.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.69,0:09:27.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are we really going to\Ngo after Ed and Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.69,0:09:29.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those are our orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.56,0:09:32.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But this was the work of Scar.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.32,0:09:34.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's also partially Archer's fault\Nfor being reckless.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.44,0:09:36.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't know what went down here,\Nbut the brothers—
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.07,0:09:38.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The fact is, they've run away.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.07,0:09:40.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we let them go, it's going to come down on the Colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.24,0:09:43.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He said that if things get out of hand,\Nthe Colonel was to kill them!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.79,0:09:47.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shall we get going, Colonel?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.21,0:09:48.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.01,0:10:39.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did you stay here again\Nall last night?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.93,0:10:41.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.89,0:10:46.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I just don't have a good grasp on my sense of the passage of time.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.39,0:10:49.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How many years has it been\Nsince Trisha died?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.15,0:10:51.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's been six years now.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.61,0:10:56.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see. The children \Nmust have grieved, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.61,0:10:59.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sara Rockbell?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.11,0:11:01.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But I thought you were Sara.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.99,0:11:05.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I told you before, remember?\NI'm Winry.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.87,0:11:08.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sara was my mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.34,0:11:18.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So that's how.\NThe war, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.01,0:11:22.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It wasn't just war.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.59,0:11:25.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They were killed.\NAnd by a soldier who would ordinarily be their ally.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.89,0:11:28.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All because they treated\Nfriends and foes impartially.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.98,0:11:31.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's so sad.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.23,0:11:35.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please don't make it\Nsound so simple.\NIt's not just sad.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.23,0:11:37.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.24,0:11:40.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,know the man who\Nkilled my parents.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.86,0:11:43.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I also know that he is\Nby no means a bad person.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.91,0:11:47.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So I can't even do\Nanything about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.99,0:11:49.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.62,0:11:53.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why it's so sad.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.23,0:12:14.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.65,0:12:17.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm so hungry!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.23,0:12:21.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,L-Lieutenant Ross!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.65,0:12:22.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And Brosh!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.61,0:12:26.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You really have come after us, haven't you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.78,0:12:29.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's because we saw something we weren't supposed to see!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.91,0:12:31.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, sure enough,\Nyou've come after us!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.63,0:12:41.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Scieszka!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.14,0:12:48.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I never knew.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.14,0:12:51.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those boys don't even have a home anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.43,0:12:55.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How do you mean, those two are being pursued by the military?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.44,0:12:59.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We got an emergency phone call,\Nfrom the east.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.19,0:13:03.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They said that by the Führer's order, we were to apprehend the Fullmetal Alchemist and his brother,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.07,0:13:07.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and that they'd been in contact with the masterminds behind the revolt in Liore.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.20,0:13:10.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are those guys doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.29,0:13:14.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Someone I'm close to in\NCommunications told me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.41,0:13:18.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Currently, a search party is being\Ndrawn up by Major General Hakuro.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.42,0:13:21.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Word has probably already gone out to local police.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.01,0:13:25.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once that happened, the Lieutenant suddenly took some leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.55,0:13:27.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And here I thought\Nthis would be a date.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.55,0:13:30.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's nice to be able to\Nbreathe the clean air, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.56,0:13:33.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How can you go to all this trouble\Njust to tell all this to a wanted man?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.89,0:13:35.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you talking about?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.14,0:13:38.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if the Führer {\i1}did{\i0} order it,\NI don't believe it!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.27,0:13:40.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How could those two be rebels?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.52,0:13:41.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh, I didn't mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.65,0:13:46.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still, we don't know whether or not \Nthe two of them are even coming here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.28,0:13:48.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, they'll come home.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.41,0:13:52.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even without a house to return to,\Nthis is still their home, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.16,0:13:55.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Besides, you're here, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.91,0:13:58.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Long ago, there weren't\Nany railroads into here.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.92,0:14:05.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There wasn't even a single road that went further east, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.97,0:14:12.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Everyone used to climb the mountain alongside that stream\Nuntil it finally let out in the east.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.56,0:14:15.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We used to play a lot\Nby that stream, long ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.43,0:14:19.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's it! If I were Ed and Al,\NI would definitely come that way.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.94,0:14:20.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks, Uncle!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.36,0:14:23.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Un...cle?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.27,0:14:23.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's go, Scieszka!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.61,0:14:24.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ross-san, you guys stay here!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.36,0:14:28.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If the search party shows up,\Nwe'll slow them down as best we can!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.53,0:14:29.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank you!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.08,0:14:36.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There weren't any\Nrailroads into here?\NBut that was over\Na hundred years ago...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.17,0:14:48.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, hide!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.68,0:14:53.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.68,0:14:55.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just take cover!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.64,0:15:02.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So ultimately, this is all\Njust about some promotion?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.48,0:15:05.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wouldn't say that's the only reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.61,0:15:06.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He said so, didn't he?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.07,0:15:08.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If the Elric brothers get away,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.07,0:15:12.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the Colonel will bear full responsibility for what happened in Liore.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.32,0:15:13.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Colonel will?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.70,0:15:16.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case, there isn't much we can do, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.33,0:15:24.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,H-Hey there, Edward-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.84,0:15:26.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just as the Colonel predicted.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.88,0:15:29.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're taking the side road to your hometown that you're used to taking.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.09,0:15:35.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.22,0:15:37.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Move.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.43,0:15:37.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed-kun?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.35,0:15:40.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm never going back to the military!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.52,0:15:45.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go ahead and fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.11,0:15:48.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,See whether or not you can\Nshoot through my Automail!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.40,0:15:49.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,E-Edward-kun, why?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.24,0:15:51.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go ahead and shoot!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.78,0:15:52.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.12,0:16:01.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Havoc-san...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.54,0:16:08.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We aren't going back.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.51,0:16:10.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.76,0:16:12.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.68,0:16:16.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come quietly!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.31,0:16:23.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward-kun!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.19,0:16:25.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you've got something to say,\Nwe're all ears!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.77,0:16:27.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We aren't your enemy!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.86,0:16:31.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can prove your innocence as much as you want to during the formal inquiry!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.40,0:16:34.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You'll be okay for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.16,0:16:39.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do those two seriously\Nmean to turn against us?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.08,0:16:41.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll find out\Nwhen we catch them.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.50,0:16:44.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nobody get cold feet next time!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.04,0:16:49.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel, um, could you \Nget into my breast pocket?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.05,0:16:56.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Take better care of yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.22,0:17:00.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They couldn't have gotten very far.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.68,0:17:03.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Probably because they can't very well\Nexpose Alphonse to the water.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.85,0:17:06.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because of his bloodseal.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.29,0:17:22.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Out of the way!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.01,0:17:40.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who was it that told you about the Elric brothers?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.76,0:17:42.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nobody.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.27,0:17:46.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you seriously think that those two are rebels?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.52,0:17:49.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll know once we catch them\Nand interrogate them.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.03,0:17:55.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You're{\i0} the one who recruited Ed and Al, aren't you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.86,0:17:56.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And now this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.49,0:17:58.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's no use.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.49,0:18:01.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The only thing this man is interested in\Nis his rank within the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.99,0:18:02.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Answer me!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.99,0:18:06.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Was this how it was when you killed my father and mother, too?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.55,0:18:21.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.47,0:18:24.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't touch me carelessly!\NWe don't know what will happen!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.08,0:18:50.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why are you running?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.09,0:18:53.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed! Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.63,0:18:54.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.30,0:18:58.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because you're chasing us, that's why.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.72,0:19:01.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When a dog is chased, he runs away.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.97,0:19:05.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A well-trained dog never\Ngoes against his master's orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.64,0:19:06.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did you say "master"?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.81,0:19:10.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or, have you suddenly\Ngone back to being a stray dog?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.65,0:19:12.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Relax, Edward-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.65,0:19:15.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if you were cursed as a dog of the military,\Nyou would put up with it\Nin order to achieve your goal.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.90,0:19:17.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Isn't that what you said?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.74,0:19:23.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm through being\Na dog of the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.66,0:19:27.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Does this mean you're going back to being\Na helpless child who won't listen to reason?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.50,0:19:29.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Call it whatever you want!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.30,0:19:37.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're slipping, Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.67,0:19:38.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.19,0:19:40.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.83,0:19:40.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.36,0:19:59.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.32,0:20:03.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I transmuted the stone projectile in mid-air...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.70,0:20:09.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...and I compressed the air within it and ignited it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.08,0:20:09.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,An effective attack, was it not?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.70,0:20:12.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That must have come in handy\Nin Ishbal, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.43,0:20:29.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.95,0:20:48.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,620)}Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.17,0:20:57.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please... stop...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.84,0:20:58.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.05,0:21:04.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once, I killed two people.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.72,0:21:08.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They were doctors.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.76,0:21:12.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There were no friends or foes\Namong their patients.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.43,0:21:14.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what they said as they treated those around the battlefield.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.81,0:21:19.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, those whom they treated became our enemies.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.57,0:21:24.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The military repeatedly asked them\Nto stop treating our enemies,\Nbut they refused to listen.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.82,0:21:28.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was given an order... and I...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.28,0:21:30.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,shot them.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.33,0:21:41.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ever since, I swore that \Neven if I were under orders,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.96,0:21:41.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I would not follow anything that was unreasonable.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.26,0:21:44.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That I would put myself in a position where I didn't have to follow them.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.14,0:21:50.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The reason I'm chasing after you is not because I was ordered to.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.93,0:21:53.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's because I'm pissed off at you!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.68,0:21:58.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why did you run off on your own\Nwithout coming to me for protection?!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.66,0:23:40.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.41,0:23:44.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 44: "Hohenheim of Light"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.25,0:23:47.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What the hell are you doing here...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.42,0:23:50.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you rotten old man?!
